---
system: sys-01-identity-household-access
flow_id: household-leave
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/01-identity-household-access#household-leave-adr-0010
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - POST /v1/household/leave
externals: []
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - cannot_leave_as_primary_transfer_first
  - last_member_cannot_leave
  - already_revoked
idempotency: idempotent on (user_id) — repeat call when already revoked returns 200
retry: single retry on 5xx
timeout: 2s
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Secondary parent leaves household per ADR-0010 D8. Primary (owner) CANNOT leave — must transfer first (references D7). Sets household_members.status=revoked + revoked_at=now(). Revokes all parent_sessions for that user. users row stays intact as orphan; user can join another household via invite.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService
    participant PostgreSQL

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/household/leave + Bearer JWT
    Gateway->>Gateway: validate parent JWT — extract user_id, household_id
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT role, status FROM household_members WHERE user_id={user_id} AND household_id={household_id}
    PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: member row or null
    alt member_not_found
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 404 member_not_found
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 404
    else already_revoked (status = 'revoked')
        Note over IdentityService: Idempotent — treat as success
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {left: true, already_revoked: true}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else cannot_leave_as_primary_transfer_first (role = 'owner')
        Note over IdentityService: ADR-0010 D8 — primary must transfer role before leaving
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 409 cannot_leave_as_primary_transfer_first {hint: 'use POST /v1/household/transfer-primary first'}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
    else last_member_cannot_leave
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM household_members WHERE household_id={household_id} AND status='active'
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: active_count
        alt active_count = 1 (would leave household empty)
            IdentityService-->>Gateway: 409 last_member_cannot_leave {hint: 'delete account instead'}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
        else secondary_can_leave
            IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE household_members SET status='revoked', revoked_at=now() WHERE user_id={user_id} AND household_id={household_id}
            PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: updated
            IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE parent_sessions SET revoked_at=now() WHERE user_id={user_id} AND revoked_at IS NULL
            PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: all sessions revoked
            Note over IdentityService: users row intact — user is now orphan (no active household_members row)
            IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {left: true, household_id}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
            ParentApp->>ParentApp: clear parent.store + Keychain + route to post-household landing screen
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 2s — idempotent on (user_id) — primary role blocked (must transfer first per ADR-0010 D8) — users row preserved as orphan after leave
